            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "My initial impression is that I don't really like the idea of mixing registers here. Can't really put that into words, though. Mostly a combination of \"it introduces another abstraction\", \"register is for contiguous charwise/linewise/blockwise text region\", and \"requires more code\", but maybe something else.\r\n\r\n> > This will populate both input and output of target surrounding\r\n> \r\n> How would `input` be helpful with other operators (seemingly replace)?\r\n\r\nSame as [user prompt](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c8bc67a35e627908da644c5f8cd26b3f987f2627/doc/mini-surround.txt#L181-L182) and would find surrounding with that exact yanked left and right edges.",
